{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790983588,"nonce":"IyzqWlC3GMM0RBq8F6JicSe9T4g=","title":"Board: wider default columns, and column_width as an argument","message":"Asked 2026-10-02 (Luis): the default kanban column is too narrow. Today minColumnWidth is 20 and columns share the width equally when they all fit, so six statuses on a 120-wide terminal are 20 cells each and titles wrap over several lines. Decided: a defaulted `column_width` argument on the board, default 32, the width below which the board scrolls sideways instead of squeezing; when every column fits at that width they still share the width equally, never narrower than the argument.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"priority":"medium","status":"in-progress","type":"task"}}]}